WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.890
Pete, I am good at asking questions. Let me ask you some.

2
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.370
Really, Anna? Can you help me?

3
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.110
Yes, I can. Let me help.

4
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:22.330
Sure, Anna. Maybe you can help.

5
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.050
Can you write code?

6
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:32.550
Sure, c-o-l-d. How is this going to help?

7
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:43.190
No, not “cold.” Code; you know, for making phone apps, or websites. You can make tons of money writing code.

8
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.690
Tons of money? But I can’t code.

9
00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:49.630
Next question. Can you drive?

10
00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:57.350
Do you mean drive a race car? It’s really hard to be a race car driver. First, you need a race car ...

11
00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.970
No, I mean drive a taxi or drive a bus.

12
00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:05.310
No, I always fall asleep when I drive.

13
00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:37.030
Oh, that’s not good. Next question. Can you teach? You can be a teacher in a school.

14
00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:39.850
No, I cannot teach.

15
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:44.850
Can you cook? You can be a chef in a restaurant.

16
00:01:49.960 --> 00:02:05.790
No, I can’t code! I can’t teach! I can’t cook! Anna, I can’t do anything. This is sad. I’m gonna write about my feelings in my blog.

17
00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.290
You write a blog?

18
00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:10.850
Yeah, I write a blog.

19
00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.690
How many followers do you have?

20
00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:15.290
I don’t know … 59,538.

21
00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:24.590
Pete, that's a lot of followers! You can make money writing!
